{
  "name": "654. A custom provider on the moonshot base prices a cache write at the requested TTL (custom provider on moonshot cache ttl pricing)",
  "description": "TXE-7996, a follow-up to TXE-7069 (folder 646). Kimi bills a cache write by the request's prompt_cache_options.ttl and reports one cached_write_tokens figure. Pricing applied the requested tier only when the request's provider was moonshot itself, so a custom provider on the moonshot base (kimi_custom) had its 1-hour write priced at the base rate. The fixture's pricing sheet has one Kimi row, moonshot/fixture-kimi-ttl-priced: $1/M input, $2/M output, $3/M cache write and $6/M cache write above an hour. /pp/ownkey answers with 3,000 prompt tokens, 2,000 of them written to the cache, and 200 completion tokens. At 1h that is $0.0134, and at 5m or no TTL $0.0074. Rows 654.1 to 654.3 send /v1/chat/completions; 654.4 and 654.5 send /v1/responses, which /pp/ownkey answers with the same usage in the Responses shape (input_tokens_details.cache_write_tokens). Against a gateway without the fix, row 654.1 is logged at $0.0074.",
  "event": [
    {
      "listen": "prerequest",
      "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "exec": [
          "if (pm.variables.get('videoSettlementFixture') !== '1') {",
          "  pm.execution.skipRequest();",
          "}"
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "654.1 kimi_custom/fixture-kimi-ttl-priced POST /v1/chat/completions with prompt_cache_options.ttl 1h is logged at $0.0134 (custom provider on moonshot cache ttl pricing)",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "prerequest",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.variables.set('kimiTtlRequestId1', 'kimi-ttl-1-' + Date.now() + '-' + Math.floor(Math.random() * 1e6));"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "var requestId = pm.variables.get('kimiTtlRequestId1');",
              "pm.test('the chat completion succeeds', function () {",
              "  pm.expect(pm.response.code, 'failed: ' + pm.response.text()).to.eql(200);",
              "});",
              "pm.test('usage carries the write as Kimi reported it, with no tier derived from the request', function () {",
              "  var d = (pm.response.json().usage || {}).prompt_tokens_details || {};",
              "  pm.expect(d.cached_write_tokens, JSON.stringify(d)).to.eql(2000);",
              "  pm.expect(d.cached_write_token_details, JSON.stringify(d)).to.be.undefined;",
              "});",
              "// The log row is written by the batching writer, so poll for it. Bounded: ten reads a second apart.",
              "var token = pm.variables.get('setupToken');",
              "function check(attempt) {",
              "  pm.sendRequest({ url: pm.variables.get('baseUrl') + '/api/logs/' + requestId, method: 'GET', header: { 'X-Bifrost-Setup-Token': token } }, function (err, res) {",
              "    if (!err && res.code === 200 && res.json().status === 'success') {",
              "      var j = res.json();",
              "      pm.test('the 2,000-token cache write is priced at the 1-hour rate', function () {",
              "        pm.expect(j.provider, JSON.stringify(j)).to.eql('kimi_custom');",
              "        pm.expect(j.cost, 'logged with no cost: ' + JSON.stringify(j)).to.be.a('number');",
              "        pm.expect(j.cost, JSON.stringify(j)).to.be.closeTo(0.0134, 1e-12);",
              "      });",
              "      return;",
              "    }",
              "    if (attempt < 10) { setTimeout(function () { check(attempt + 1); }, 1000); return; }",
              "    pm.test('the log row appeared', function () { pm.expect.fail('log ' + requestId + ' never appeared: ' + (err ? String(err) : (res.code + ' ' + res.text()))); });",
              "  });",
              "}",
              "check(0);"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          },
          {
            "key": "x-request-id",
            "value": "{{kimiTtlRequestId1}}"
          }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/chat/completions",
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "v1",
            "chat",
            "completions"
          ]
        },
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\"model\": \"kimi_custom/fixture-kimi-ttl-priced\", \"messages\": [{\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"hi\"}], \"prompt_cache_options\": {\"ttl\": \"1h\"}}"
        }
      }
    },
